        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Tribometer\n- People: Pieter van Musschenbroek\n- Concepts: Tribological quantities, coefficient of friction, friction force, wear volume\n\nFacts:\n- Pieter van Musschenbroek was a Dutch scientist who lived from 14 March 1692 to 19 September 1761.\n- In the 18th century, Pieter van Musschenbroek invented the tribometer.\n- A tribometer is an instrument that measures tribological quantities between two surfaces in contact.\n- A tribometer can measure quantities such as coefficient of friction, friction force, and wear volume.",
